From: Try FydeOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu-virgl: flush the GL context after a 2D upload

Applies after Try Omarchy's QEMU patches.

The guest's 2D path (frecon, the firmware console) uploads its framebuffer
with TRANSFER_TO_HOST_2D, which virglrenderer turns into a texture
sub-image upload in its own GL context. Nothing flushes that context: the
renderer only flushes when a client creates a fence, and the kernel's 2D
path never does. The Cocoa display samples the same texture from a second
context, so it keeps showing the last flushed contents. Small uploads
happen to get through the driver at once; a full backing-size console
framebuffer does not, and typed characters only appear after the next
modeset. Flush right after the upload, while the renderer's context is
current.

--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -664,6 +664,12 @@ static void virgl_cmd_transfer_to_host_2d(VirtIOGPU *g,
                                       0,
                                       (struct virgl_box *)&box,
                                       t2d.offset, NULL, 0);
+    /*
+     * A 2D upload carries no fence, so nothing flushes it out of the
+     * renderer's context before the display samples the texture from its
+     * own context.
+     */
+    glFlush();
 }
 
 static void virgl_cmd_transfer_to_host_3d(VirtIOGPU *g,
